{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-06T11:33:09.523Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"e5330e1791f32ab2f4c04d76","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"argv"},"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.319","source":"probe"}},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-gh1679"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"GH-1679: SDK and CLI item history have no producer cursor, so paging backwards through a long history requests an ever-larger newest suffix per page"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"GitHub issue #1679 (reported 2026-11-06 against 2026.11.5 from an SDK adoption review of the fleet). HistoryCommandOptions exposes limit and order but no producer cursor, and HistoryResult returns no continuation (dist/sdk/query/history.d.ts). Public output cursors page an already-produced projection, so they do not bound the historical read. A consumer paging backwards through a long item history must request an ever-larger newest suffix for each older page, then verify and filter it. The concrete consumer is pm-web's item-history panel (src/services/item-history.ts), which requests successively larger suffixes. Proposal: opaque bounded backwards and forwards item-history paging in the SDK and CLI. The continuation is bound to the item, order, projection and a verified stream boundary. Each page returns bounded rows, explicit completeness and omission receipts, and a safe stale_cursor refusal. Pages stay stable under appends where safe, and compaction, rewrite or truncation ambiguities are refused. The producer cursor stays distinct from the output cursor contract. Duplicate check: searched history cursor paging; pm-c3aiik (GH-1325, closed) fixed history diff cursor advancement, pm-dfg0 (closed) list/search/context cursors, pm-8s53lj (open) newest-page retention for comments/notes, pm-tuadp2 (open) delta projections, GH-1470 replay infrastructure. None provides a producer cursor over one item's history stream. No benchmark was run; evidence is declaration and consumer-code analysis."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":2},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["cursor","gh:1679","history","pm-web","scale","sdk"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-11-06T11:33:09.523Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-06T11:33:09.523Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"harness:claude-code"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/estimated_minutes","value":300},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"HistoryCommandOptions accepts an opaque producer cursor for backwards and forwards paging and HistoryResult returns a continuation bound to the item, order, projection and a verified stream boundary; Each page reads a bounded number of entries regardless of history length, proven by a work-bound spec over a long history; Concurrent appends between pages neither skip nor duplicate certified rows, and a cursor for another item, a tampered cursor, or a stream compacted or rewritten since issue is refused with a typed stale_cursor error; The producer cursor is distinct from the output cursor contract and works in JSON and TOON through CLI, SDK and MCP"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-9rgaal"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/risk","value":"medium"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/confidence","value":"medium"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/dependencies","value":[{"id":"pm-8s53lj","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-11-06T11:33:09.523Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-c3aiik","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-11-06T11:33:09.523Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"}]}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"6c156dccc4e14b144b5d83f764a7ef809b08f0fcc138238dbad05ae1a095a43e","item_hash_version":3,"message":"","context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"02222af4456c282d543136a7c9ec26cfeab9041cf16b10b47414d0c62ab13fcd"}
